{
  "description": "Status lines a PLC bridge writes on stdout under --status-lines (ADR 0050 point 2, ADR 0065 points 5 and 7). Each entry is one JSON line: `message` is the decoded line, `text` a line that is not JSON. The Modbus bridge must emit lines equal to every `valid` entry that names its transport (`ready`) or one of its exit kinds (`exiting`, certificate and module null); the OPC UA bridge does the same for its own. The core's Zod schema must accept every `valid` entry and refuse every `invalid` one. A line over maxLineBytes is a log line, not a status line.",
  "version": 2,
  "maxLineBytes": 4096,
  "exitKinds": [
    "configuration",
    "core_unavailable",
    "mapping_not_valid",
    "mapping_changed",
    "bus_closed",
    "protocol",
    "unexpected",
    "untrusted_server_certificate",
    "server_certificate_invalid",
    "authentication_failed"
  ],
  "valid": [
